      "worked": "The shortest distance is along the perpendicular to $y=2x$ through $A(0,5)$. Its gradient is $-\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-5&=-\\frac12(x-0)\\\\2y-10&=-x\\\\x+2y&=10.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt the intersection, $y=2x$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2(2x)&=10\\\\5x&=10\\\\x&=2\\\\y&=2x\\\\y&=2(2)\\\\y&=4.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe required point is $P(2,4)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
